course: dictionary
lesson: 8372
title: What is a router?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A router is a small box that connects your computers, phones and tablets to the internet, and to each other. «A Wi-Fi router is a small radio station that talks to your devices by radio.» The router is the middle point between your devices and the wider internet.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another subject. A router can also be a power tool that cuts shapes and grooves in wood. Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about data, Wi-Fi or the internet, it means the box. If it talks about wood and cutting, it means the tool.
explain: Look at «Theo decided he was a tech genius and turned the router off and on forty times in one evening.» Turning a router off and on again is a common fix when the Wi-Fi stops, so the router here is the box. Test your meaning: "a wood-cutting tool" makes no sense in this sentence, so you know which meaning fits.
fact: A router is a small box that connects your devices to the internet and to each other.
fact: Messages are turned into bits and split into packets, which are small chunks of data.
fact: A router passes packets on towards where they are going, one step at a time.
fact: «Restart the router» means turn it off and on again.
fact: In woodwork, a router is a power tool that cuts shapes and grooves in wood.
exercise: «Theo turned the router off and on forty times.» What is a router in this sentence? | A kind of bird that lives in trees | A computer game | A tool that cuts grooves in wood | *A small box that connects devices to the internet
exercise: Dad says, «The router needs a restart.» What does restart mean here? | *Turn it off and on again | Take it to the shop to be sold | Put it in a cupboard for ever | Paint it bright red
exercise: «A Wi-Fi router is a small radio station that talks to your devices by radio.» What does a Wi-Fi router talk to? | Only the sky | Wooden tables | Mirrors and fish tanks | *Your devices, by radio
test: «The carpenter used a router to cut a neat groove in the table.» What is a router in this sentence? | *A power tool that cuts grooves in wood | A box that connects phones to the internet | A radio station for birds | A bag for holding tools
test: «Messages are split into packets, and a router passes them towards where they are going.» What does a router do with packets? | Cuts them into wooden shapes | Turns them into sea water | Stores them in a cupboard for ever | *Passes them on towards where they are going
exam: Ava's text: «Her phone turns the message into bits, and routers pass them on hop by hop until they reach nan's phone.» Which best describes the routers in this sentence? | Tools for cutting wood | *Boxes that pass data on towards its destination | Big buildings full of fans and servers | Shops that sell phones
